@startuml e2e_error_handling_state_machine

title "E2E State Machine — sm_state wiring (E2E spec §4.3/§4.4, R5)"

state E2E_SM_DEINIT as "Deinit" : state machine not yet started
state E2E_SM_NODATA as "NoData" : waiting for the first reception
state E2E_SM_INIT as "Init" : accumulating checkStatus over WindowSizeInit
state E2E_SM_VALID as "Valid" : ok to use the data
state E2E_SM_INVALID as "Invalid" : genuine communication fault

[*] --> E2E_SM_DEINIT
E2E_SM_DEINIT --> E2E_SM_NODATA : enabled / first E2E_SMCheck() call

E2E_SM_NODATA --> E2E_SM_INIT : first sample received (R5: NOT a fault)
E2E_SM_NODATA --> E2E_SM_INVALID : transitToInvalidExtended\n&& error before any reception

E2E_SM_INIT --> E2E_SM_VALID : MinOkStateInit reached\nwithin WindowSizeInit (R5: NOT a fault)
E2E_SM_INIT --> E2E_SM_INVALID : transitToInvalidExtended\n&& MaxErrorStateInit reached

E2E_SM_VALID --> E2E_SM_INVALID : MaxErrorStateValid reached\nwithin WindowSizeValid (genuine fault)
E2E_SM_INVALID --> E2E_SM_VALID : MinOkStateInvalid reached\nwithin WindowSizeInvalid

note right of E2E_SM_NODATA
  NoData/Init are warm-up states, driven by
  E2E_SMCheck()'s configured sliding-window
  and threshold parameters (WindowSizeInit/
  Valid/Invalid, MinOkState*, MaxErrorState*)
  — never a fixed single-sample rule.
  Proposal decision (§3 of e2eerror handling.md):
  sm_state is exposed alongside checkStatus so the
  caller distinguishes "not enough history yet"
  from a genuine Invalid fault, instead of an
  ad-hoc first-sample suppression rule.
end note

note right of E2E_SM_INVALID
  clearFromValidToInvalid config controls whether
  the whole monitoring window is cleared or merely
  extended on a Valid → Invalid transition.
end note

note bottom of E2E_SM_DEINIT
  disableEndToEndStateMachine = true: skip this
  state machine entirely; caller only receives the
  raw per-sample checkStatus (no smState).
end note

@enduml
